    "result_text": "The build succeeded with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a two-stage points system.\n\n**`MembershipLevel.java`** (`src/main/java/.../mapper/`) \u2014 now exposes:\n- `points(Owner)` \u2014 starts at 0, then **+2** email present, **+1** `namesakeCount == 0`, **+2** household of 3+ (`householdSize >= 3`), **+3** tenure over 365 days.\n- `of(Owner)` \u2014 maps points to level: **1** (0\u20131), **2** (2\u20133), **3** (4\u20135), **4** (6+).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipPoints` mapping alongside the existing `membershipLevel`, so both fields are returned.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema field and updated `membershipLevel` (now 1\u20134, derived from points) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries both.\n\n**`LogOwnerAudit.java`** \u2014 audit line now logs both `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel` from the single source of truth.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest` (fresh owner with email, no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure \u2192 3 points \u2192 level 2) passes, and the full suite is **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
