    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, read from `owners.POST.yml` and each function class. I've marked which steps **validate** (can reject) versus produce a **side-effect** (mutate the DTO/entity, hit the DB, or log).\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the whole endpoint is guarded by `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. A caller without that role is denied (`AuthorizationDeniedException`) before the pipeline runs.\n\n## Ordered steps\n\n1. **RequireOwnerFields** \u2014 *validation*. Binds the request body once (`OwnerFieldsDto`, no `@Valid`). Rejects **400** (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`, listing every offender) if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, or `telephone` is null/blank, or if `address` is blank *after normalization*. Republishes the DTO as a variable for later steps.\n\n2. **RequireCurrentRegistrationDate** \u2014 *validation*. Only if `registrationDate` is present: rejects **400** (`FutureRegistrationDateException`) when the supplied date is after today. Absent date is left alone.\n\n3. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 *side-effect + validation*. Normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep `+`+country code or assume `+61` and drop a leading `0`; require 8\u201315 digits, and correct national length for known codes \u2014 `+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Writes the E.164 value back onto the DTO. Rejects **400** (`InvalidTelephoneException`) if it can't form valid E.164.\n\n4. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 *side-effect + validation*. `email` is optional: null/blank is set to `null`. If present, trims and validates syntax; writes back the trimmed, lower-cased value. Rejects **400** (`InvalidEmailException`) if present-but-invalid.\n\n5. **RequireEmailDomain** \u2014 *validation*. If an email is present, rejects **400** (`DisposableEmailDomainException`) when its domain is on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n\n6. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** \u2014 *side-effect*. Rewrites `address` to canonical form (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`) back onto the DTO.\n\n7. **RequirePostcode** \u2014 *validation*. Only if `postcode` present: must be 4 digits, and for a city with a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) must fall in range. Rejects **400** (`InvalidPostcodeException`) otherwise. Unknown-region city accepts any 4 digits.\n\n--- *transaction begins here (`govern: [ transaction ]` from this step onward)* ---\n\n8. **RequireUniqueIdentity** \u2014 *validation* (reads all owners). Computes a deterministic `householdId` (from last name + postcode) and an `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`). Rejects **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`) if the full identity key matches any existing owner, or if the `householdId` matches an existing owner *unless* the request set `sharesHousehold: true`.\n\n9. **RequireCityCapacity** \u2014 *validation* (reads all owners). Rejects **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`) if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners.\n\n10. **RequireDailyCapacity** \u2014 *validation* (reads all owners). Computes the effective registration date (supplied-or-today, rolled to next business day) and rejects **429** (`DailyLimitExceededException`) if \u2265 100 existing owners already carry that date.\n\n11. **BuildOwner** \u2014 *side-effect*. Maps the validated DTO into a new `Owner` entity (published as a variable).\n\n12. **AssignHouseholdId** \u2014 *side-effect*. Stamps the deterministic `householdId` (last name + postcode) on the owner; null when there's no postcode.\n\n13. **CountHouseholdMembers** \u2014 *side-effect* (reads all owners). Sets `householdSize` = existing owners with the same `householdId` + 1 (the new owner). Left null if no household.\n\n14. **ApplyRegistrationDate** \u2014 *side-effect*. Sets the owner's `registrationDate` to the effective date (supplied-or-today, rolled forward off weekends).\n\n15. **AssignCustomerCode** \u2014 *side-effect*. Sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where REGION comes from postcode-then-city (`Locality`) and HASH8 is the first 8 hex chars of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n\n16. **CountNamesakes** \u2014 *side-effect* (reads all owners). Sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n17. **FlagBulkSignup** \u2014 *side-effect* (reads all owners). Sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true when > 80 existing owners already carry this registration date.\n\n18. **FlagPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 *side-effect* (reads all owners). Defaults `possibleDuplicate=false`/`possibleDuplicateOf=null`. Unless `sharesHousehold` was declared or there's no postcode, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf`=earliest matching owner id when an existing owner shares last name + postcode but has a different telephone.\n\n19. **SaveOwner** \u2014 *side-effect*. Persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (generates its id).\n\n20. **LogOwnerAudit** \u2014 *side-effect*. Emits an `AUDIT` log line with id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and computed membership points/level.\n\n21. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 *side-effect (response)*. Maps the saved owner to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nThe whole span from step 8 commits once at the end (single write transaction). Any escalation thrown along the way is mapped to its status by the matching handler under `officefloor/escalation/`; anything unmatched falls through to Spring's `@RestControllerAdvice`."
